  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging over the western U.S. will remain in place in\nvarying degrees through at least Saturday. Hot weather will\ncontinue into the weekend. Today will be somewhat hotter with many\nareas in the east between 100 and 105 for highs and heat impact\nreaching into major in some of the 100+ areas. Will issue a Heat\nAdvisory for several zones in the east today. \n\nSmoke from western Montana and Pacific NW wildfires will continue\nto be over the area today and tonight with unhealthy air quality\nat times and variable visibility. \n\nWeak waves will move through the ridge at various times through \nThursday night with chances for showers and thunderstorms over \nparts of the region. Models are showing increased instability and \nhigher dew points this afternoon and evening with a cool front \nmoving through that could lead to a few severe thunderstorms. SPC \nhas a slight risk mainly east of the Yellowstone River today with \na threat of large hail and damaging winds. Additional chances for\nshowers and thunderstorms continue late tonight through Thursday\nnight over eastern Montana with a surface low over the area. \n\nHigh on Thursday will be 5 to 10 degrees lower before the ridge \nstrengthen Friday and Saturday. At this point, Saturday looks like\nit will be very hot with highs above 100 in most areas.\n\nRidge moves east Saturday night and upper trough moves for Sunday\nand Monday. A strong dry cold front on Sunday is expected to bring\ngusty NW winds followed by much cooler temperatures on Monday.  \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nHigh confidence in the hot weather continuing through Saturday. \nLow confidence in timing any showers and thunderstorms.\n\nDeviated from the NBM to tweak pops at times this afternoon \nthrough Thursday to provide better hour to hour consistency and \nbetter match SPC Outlooks for convection.",
